  "raw": "{\"judgements\":[{\"id\":\"T1\",\"kind\":\"consequential_gap\",\"quotes\":[\"Here and in rule 2 the path is opened component by component without\\nfollowing a symbolic link at any of them, each component with Linux's\\n`O_NOFOLLOW`, whose presence no code tests (A20 rule 3) — the path as\\ngiven, an absolute one walked from the root directory and a relative one\\nfrom the working directory; each directory on the way opened with\\n`O_PATH` and `O_DIRECTORY`, so a directory the kernel's user may only\\nsearch is passed, and the last component for reading; every component the\\npath names, `.` and `..` included, opened as named, and an empty one, from\\na repeated or trailing `/`, skipped; a component that cannot be opened so,\\nfor whatever reason, making the file one that cannot be read —, and the checks and the read use\\nthat one opened file, so the file checked is the file read.\",\"read_configuration: [VALIDATION_ERROR] MUST raise InstallationRejectedError naming the first failing check, in this order: config_path cannot be opened component by component without following a symbolic link at any component, each component with os.O_NOFOLLOW, whose presence is never tested, each directory on the way also with os.O_PATH and os.O_DIRECTORY (A17), the file so opened is not a regular file, is not owned by the process's effective user, or grants any permission to group or others; the bytes cannot be read or do not parse as one JSON object whose members are exactly the fields of Installation with their types; a service appears twice in service_instances or in service_credentials; a credential header name is not an HTTP field-name token (one or more of the token characters of RFC 9110: letters, digits and the symbols allowed there); a credential's secret_file is not an absolute path; the owner token or any agent token is shorter than the imported ACCESS_TOKEN_LENGTH_MIN constant; two tokens among the owner token and the agent tokens are equal; two agent tokens have the same name. The ownership, mode and regular-file checks and the read MUST all use that one opened file, so the file checked is the file read.\",\"`refused` naming the failing check; the start stops.\"],\"later_state\":null,\"precedent\":null,\"divergence\":\"One implementation rejects `/`, `//`, or an empty relative path immediately because there is no file component to open; another treats the already-open root or working directory as the target and rejects it at the regular-file check. The owner notices a different named failure on the host's start error output.\",\"why\":\"The traversal rule skips every empty component but does not define whether the starting directory becomes the target or absence of a final component is itself the first failing check.\"}]}",
